{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"41ebf22a-7a38-41d5-87a6-3a4f2aba1667:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"assistant","source":"assistant_message","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"assistant_message\",\"text\":\"# 🌟 Living Fleet: your servers are now pets, neglect is now animal cruelty\\n\\n## TL;DR\\n\\nInfra Pilot could already deploy, monitor, back up, and resurrect your containers. But it had one fatal flaw: **nobody loved them.** This PR fixes that. Every workload now gets a living creature whose mood is derived 100% from real telemetry. No mood swings without a metric to blame.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- 🧠 **Mood engine** (`services/orchestrator-agent/living_fleet.py`) — five vitals (`health`, `energy`, `hunger`, `hygiene`, `morale`), one closed mood enum, zero randomness. The creature doesn't get sad because Mercury is in retrograde. It gets sad because you haven't deployed in 47 days, Kevin.\\n- 🔌 **Fleet API** — `GET /api/v1/fleet/creatures`, detail view with a full \\\"why does it feel like this?\\\" explanation trace, plus one (1) allowed mutation: rename. You may pet the creature. You may name the creature. You may NOT gaslight the creature.\\n- 💬 **Discord** — `/pet` lists your menagerie, `/pet-status` shows vitals. Your homelab group chat is about to become a daycare with opinions.\\n- ⌨️ **CLI** — `ipilot pet list/status/rename`, for operators who show affection through terminals.\\n- 🖼️ **Panel** — `<FleetPet>` component exists and is adorable. It is currently unmounted, sitting in a box like a shelter puppy waiting for `AppCard` to adopt it (mount TODO in the file).\\n- 📋 **The plan** (`docs/LIVING-FLEET-PLAN.md`) — the full design doc, non-goals included. Yes, \\\"no blockchain/NFT anything. Ever.\\\" is in there. Someone had to say it.\\n\\n## The emotional lifecycle\\n\\n| Mood | Meaning |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| 🌟 thriving | 99.9% uptime, touched grass, evolved |\\n| 😊 content | healthy, boring, the dream |\\n| 😴 sleepy | idle so long it started dreaming of packets |\\n| 🍽️ hungry | hasn't been deployed in a month, rattling its bowl |\\n| 🤒 sick | crash-looping, has the sniffles (the sniffles are OOMKills) |\\n| 😰 stressed | CPU at 97%, needs a juice box and a smaller workload |\\n| 😢 sad | some vital dipped under 50, general disappointment in you |\\n| 👻 ghost | down 6+ hours unacknowledged. It haunts your dashboard now. This is your fault. |\\n\\n## ⚠️ Honest fine print (CI, this means you)\\n\\n- Barecode v0, **untested locally** — nothing was installed or executed. The sandbox and I have an understanding, and the understanding is fear.\\n- Nothing calls `refresh()` yet — the engine is a brain with no senses. Signal collection + birth hooks are the next PR.\\n- Feature is gated behind `LIVING_FLEET_ENABLED` (default off), so main stays calm and creature-free until we're ready.\\n- Branch: `feature/living-fleet-barecode`. Main was not harmed in the making of this PR.\\n\\n## Test plan\\n\\n1. Enable the gate, watch creatures be born 🥚\\n2. Deploy something → creature feasts 🍽️→😊\\n3. Ignore something for a month → guilt 👻\\n4. Run the suite, confirm zero regressions and at least one developer emotionally compromised\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Infra Pilot: now with 100% more attachment issues.* 🐾\",\"provider_item_id\":\"msg_01a165915ea5735ca9cb275d146e57b9\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}","truncated":false}
